 "template": "On the Grafana dashboard '{{v1}} {{v2}} Dashboard' (saved, time range 'Last 6 hours', tag 'bench'), set the dashboard's auto-refresh interval to '1m'. Use the refresh-interval control in the top bar (the clock/refresh dropdown next to the time range picker) and select '1m'. Then make sure this refresh interval is PERSISTED into the saved dashboard: check whether the dashboard now shows unsaved changes (Save dashboard button enabled / dirty indicator); if so, save the dashboard via the Save dashboard button, TICKING the 'Update default time range' checkbox in the save dialog (so the 6-hour range stays persisted), and confirm '{{02-create.save_confirmation}}'. If changing the picker does not mark the dashboard dirty, find another way to persist the 1m refresh interval into the saved dashboard (e.g. a setting in Dashboard settings) and save. Finally verify persistence: fully reload the dashboard URL with NO query params and confirm the refresh interval control still shows '1m' and the time range still shows 'Last 6 hours'. Report: the refresh interval shown after reload, the time range shown after reload, and exactly how you persisted the refresh interval.",
