  "summary": "Set the top-bar refresh picker to '1m' on '{{v1}} {{v2}} Dashboard'. The picker change alone did not mark the dashboard dirty (the Save dashboard dialog said \"No changes to save\"), so I entered edit mode (Edit), opened Save dashboard, ticked the \"Update default refresh value – Will make the current refresh the new default\" checkbox (which registered \"Changes 1\" and enabled Save) — the \"Update default time range\" checkbox was not offered because the current 6-hour range already equalled the saved default — and clicked Save, which confirmed with the \"Dashboard saved\" alert and closed edit mode. Verified persistence by reloading the bare URL /d/bfy6g8hcxk3k0c/{{v1}}-bench-dashboard with no query params: the refresh control shows '1m' and the time picker shows 'Last 6 hours' (Grafana re-added from=now-6h&refresh=1m from the saved defaults). The replay's failed step 4 (ticking \"Update default refresh value\") was completed manually.",
